35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,The lab is down to one person with two hundred pieces waiting. That is a heavy burden for one soul.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, one person cannot save a broken display. My data shows seventeen call-outs, four during opening hours. The bay was roped off.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"@Shion, those call-outs are painful, but my comment slips say people return for the human touch, not the hardware.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The bay is capped at four hundred kilos per square metre. Last season, stonework needed shoring. We must respect that limit.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"@Shion, seventeen call-outs! That sounds like a broken toy. But my transport costs are the real monster, taking a third of the budget!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Sakura, a third of the budget is indeed alarming. But with only one conservator, we must ask who will actually handle the fragile pieces.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Sakura, transport is a fixed cost. The real risk is the powered displays failing mid-show. I will check the maintenance log to see what actually breaks.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Sakura, a third of the budget is scary, but my head counts show crowds vanish when the room is static. We need movement, not just expensive crates.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Sakura, the budget is tight, but the floor is not. I also found the gallery is hired out six evenings a season. That limits our setup window.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Misaki, six evenings gone! That squeezes our setup time. But @Shion, if the displays break, the repair bills will join the transport monster!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, six evenings lost to hires is a real squeeze. With one conservator, we must plan for a very gentle, slow installation.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, six evenings lost means zero buffer. If a crate misses the cut-off, we are dead in the water. I will not gamble on that.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Misaki, six evenings gone is a tight squeeze. But my data says the crowd needs a living room, not a static one.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shion, you are right. The buffer is gone. I will not promise a space that cannot absorb the weight or the schedule.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Shion, I agree! No buffer means no mistakes. But remember, my mount-making data says bringing our own supports saves a fortune. Let us pick something self-contained!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
